 ## Overview
-The VStudio Framework is a software tool for interactive volume visualization that implements single-pass GPU ray casting, allowing for interactive shader editing and customization of the rendering pipeline [S1]. It distinguishes itself from other hardware-accelerated methods by exposing the full ray casting shader code (vertex and fragment components) for real-time modification, enabling users to define custom transfer functions, shading models, and traversal logic directly within the application [S1]. Unlike methods that rely on fixed-function hardware pipelines or pre-baked textures, VStudio computes ray casting on the fly using a modular shader architecture [S1].
+The VStudio Framework is an interactive volume visualization environment that performs single-pass GPU ray casting, allowing for real-time shader editing and customization of the rendering pipeline [S1]. It distinguishes itself from other hardware-accelerated methods by providing a modular, file-based shader architecture where the vertex and fragment shaders are loaded, linked, and modified at runtime via a GUI, rather than being hardcoded into the application [S1]. Unlike methods that require pre-compiled binaries, VStudio exposes the full ray casting logic to the user through separate component files for classification, gradient calculation, lighting, and shadowing [S1].
 
